0	482	Pádraig Flynn (born 9 May 1939) is an Irish former Fianna Fáil politician who served as European Commissioner for Social Affairs from 1993 to 1999, Minister for Industry and Commerce and Minister for 
483	568	He served as a Teachta Dála (TD) for the Mayo West constituency from 1977 to 1994.



568	629	Early life
Flynn was born in Castlebar, County Mayo, in 1939.
630	670	He is the son of Patrick and Anne Flynn.
671	813	He was educated in St. Gerald's College, Castlebar and qualified as a primary school teacher from St Patrick's College of Education in Dublin.
814	857	His mother owned a small shop in Castlebar.
858	950	He was married in 1963, to Dorothy and they have four children, one son and three daughters.
